<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16944" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτᾰλαίπωρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not painstaking,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτως ἀ. τοῖς πολλοῖς ἡ ζήτησις τῆς
					ἀληθείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.20
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως, οὕτως αὐτοῖς ἀ. ἡ ποίησις
					διέκειτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					254
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀ. τινὰς χειροῦσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					49.35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. διάγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀκούειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simp.
					<u>in Cael.</u>
					143.16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>not given to hard work,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>; <i>lazy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθρωπάρια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					1.29.55
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>incapable of bearing fatigue,</i> Prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				21
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως</span>”
				<i>without incurring fatigue,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Acut.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of stagnant
			water, <i>sluggish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				5.3.1
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτακτ-πώρητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.28
			</span></i>; <i>easy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.11
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοίκτως</span>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				204
			</span></i>.</div>
